{"provenance": "PaySim SIMULATOR output \u2014 synthetic transactions from aggregated real mobile-money logs (Kaggle ealaxi/paysim1, CC-BY-SA-4.0). ShareAlike applies to these bundled rows.", "licence": "CC-BY-SA-4.0", "licence_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "attribution": "E. A. Lopez-Rojas, A. Elmir and S. Axelsson, 'PaySim: A financial mobile money simulator for fraud detection', 28th European Modeling and Simulation Symposium (EMSS), Larnaca, Cyprus, 2016. Data: Kaggle ealaxi/paysim1.", "modifications": "400 rows drawn class-balanced from the bundled data/finance/paysim_sample.tsv (itself a fraud-enriched subset of the Kaggle file), whose eight columns are quantities computed from PaySim fields under AML-style names; `samples` keeps 4 of them, standardised and rounded to 5 decimals, and samples_by_space.raw the same 4, unstandardised and rounded to 5 decimals. Adapted Material, shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "names": ["amount", "cross_border", "night_tx", "new_payee"], "feature_definitions": {"amount": "log(1 + amount), the transaction amount in local currency", "cross_border": "1 if the PaySim transaction type is TRANSFER or CASH_OUT, else 0; PaySim records no geography, and its fraudulent agents transfer funds to another account and then cash out", "night_tx": "1 if the PaySim step (one simulated hour) falls in hours 0 to 5 of its day, else 0; PaySim gives step 0 no clock time, so reading those hours as night assumes it is midnight", "new_payee": "1 if the transaction is the first row of the PaySim file to name its destination account, else 0"}, "excluded_features": {"device_risk": "1 if newbalanceOrig differs from oldbalanceOrg - amount by more than 0.01; built from PaySim's origin balance columns, which the dataset's description says must not be used for fraud detection because fraudulent transactions are cancelled", "geo_mismatch": "|amount - (newbalanceDest - oldbalanceDest)| / (amount + 1), clipped to [0, 1]; built from PaySim's destination balance columns, which the dataset's description says must not be used for fraud detection for the same reason", "amount_zscore": "a z-score of log(1 + amount), so an affine copy of `amount`", "velocity_24h": "prior transactions by the same origin account within 24 steps; non-zero in 2 of the 4,000 rows of the bundled sample, and in none of the 400 the browser ships"}, "exclusion_source": {"quote": "Transactions which are detected as fraud are cancelled, so for fraud detection these columns (oldbalanceOrg, newbalanceOrig, oldbalanceDest, newbalanceDest) must not be used.", "url": "https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ealaxi/paysim1", "applies_to": ["device_risk", "geo_mismatch"]}, "samples": [[0.47463, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [1.0728, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-1.22449, -1.63836, -0.37177, 0.9649], [1.46038, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [2.01771, 0.61037, 2.68985, -1.03638], [0.21116, 0.61037, 2.68985, 0.9649], [0.11332, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [0.18101, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [0.31574, -1.63836, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-0.01149, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [1.68961, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [0.70042, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [-0.30395, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [0.94206, 0.61037, 2.68985, 0.9649], [0.372, -1.63836, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-0.32849, -1.63836, -0.37177, -1.03638], [1.71744, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-0.43093, -1.63836, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-0.76527, -1.63836, -0.37177, 0.9649], [-1.29861, 0.61037, 2.68985, -1.03638], [1.99273, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [-0.64607, -1.63836, -0.37177, -1.03638], [0.38188, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-2.17758, -1.63836, -0.37177, 0.9649], [0.10162, -1.63836, -0.37177, -1.03638], [0.29561, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [0.00911, 0.61037, 2.68985, -1.03638], [1.11867, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [0.51119, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [0.62459, 0.61037, -0.37177, 0.9649], [0.20234, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-0.24663, 0.61037, -0.37177, -1.03638], [-0.07907, 0.61037, -0.37177, 